  message: "Cross-ref backfill (2026-05-30, deeper-issue investigation): same \"field declared but never populated\" mechanic as INV-virik (failed_files/warnings/classification_failures/ambiguous_paths) and the already-linked INV-nuzal (edge.provenance/quality 100% empty). Specifically: AnalysisRun.skipped_passes (ir.py:204) is declared but `grep -n \"run.skipped_passes\\|\\.skipped_passes\\.append\" packages/hypergumbo-core/src/` finds zero producer writes. limits.skipped_passes is wired (66 entries from analyze/all_analyzers.py:80,151). The two-channel split (pass-level vs sub-unit-level) was intentional design; the sub-unit producer never landed. INV-virik should subsume this as a 5th declared-empty field."  # 27e5
